{
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "section-1",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "title": "Historia del metodo cientifico",
      "level": 1,
      "order": 1,
      "heading_type": "markdown",
      "numbering": null,
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "chunks": []
    },
    {
      "section_id": "section-2",
      "parent_section_id": "section-1",
      "title": "Introduccion",
      "level": 2,
      "order": 2,
      "heading_type": "markdown",
      "numbering": null,
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 5,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-1",
          "parent_section_id": "section-2",
          "text": "El metodo cientifico es una forma organizada de construir conocimiento mediante observacion, hipotesis, experimentacion y revision de resultados.",
          "order": 1,
          "start_line": 5,
          "end_line": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "section-3",
      "parent_section_id": "section-1",
      "title": "1. Observacion",
      "level": 2,
      "order": 3,
      "heading_type": "markdown",
      "numbering": "1",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 9,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-2",
          "parent_section_id": "section-3",
          "text": "La observacion identifica un fenomeno o problema. En esta etapa se registran patrones, preguntas y condiciones relevantes.",
          "order": 2,
          "start_line": 9,
          "end_line": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "section-4",
      "parent_section_id": "section-3",
      "title": "1.1 Hipotesis",
      "level": 3,
      "order": 4,
      "heading_type": "markdown",
      "numbering": "1.1",
      "start_line": 11,
      "end_line": 13,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-3",
          "parent_section_id": "section-4",
          "text": "Una hipotesis propone una explicacion tentativa. Debe poder ponerse a prueba y generar predicciones claras.",
          "order": 3,
          "start_line": 13,
          "end_line": 13
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "section-5",
      "parent_section_id": "section-3",
      "title": "1.2 Experimentacion",
      "level": 3,
      "order": 5,
      "heading_type": "markdown",
      "numbering": "1.2",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 17,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-4",
          "parent_section_id": "section-5",
          "text": "La experimentacion compara resultados esperados con resultados observados. Un buen experimento controla variables y permite repetir el procedimiento.",
          "order": 4,
          "start_line": 17,
          "end_line": 17
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "section-6",
      "parent_section_id": "section-1",
      "title": "2. Conclusion",
      "level": 2,
      "order": 6,
      "heading_type": "markdown",
      "numbering": "2",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 21,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "chunk-5",
          "parent_section_id": "section-6",
          "text": "Los temas importantes son observacion, hipotesis, evidencia, experimentacion y revision. La ciencia avanza cuando sus explicaciones pueden corregirse con nueva evidencia.",
          "order": 5,
          "start_line": 21,
          "end_line": 21
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "orphan_chunks": [],
  "section_count": 6,
  "subsection_count": 5,
  "chunk_count": 5
}
